---
interface Props{kind:'split'|'loop'|'diagnose'}
const {kind}=Astro.props;
const labels={split:['Three data roles; three different permissions','Figure 1. Training data fits preprocessing and parameters. Validation data helps choose settings and checkpoints. A separate test evaluates the frozen choice. This chapter includes only training and validation examples.'],loop:['Keep the update path separate from validation','Figure 2. A training batch produces gradients and an optimizer update. Validation uses current weights to measure performance without changing them. Its result can select a checkpoint or trigger a stopping rule.'],diagnose:['A curve is a clue, not a diagnosis','Figure 3. Verify the measurement before interpreting the pattern. Change one suspected cause, rerun on the same development split, and compare both quality and training cost.']};const id='training-'+kind;
---
<figure class="diagram"><div class="figure-title"><span class="figure-icon" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>{labels[kind][0]}</div><div class="diagram-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={labels[kind][0]}><svg viewBox="0 0 760 260" role="img" aria-labelledby={id+'-title '+id+'-desc'}><title id={id+'-title'}>{labels[kind][0]}</title><desc id={id+'-desc'}>{labels[kind][1]}</desc><defs><marker id={id+'-arrow'} markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" refX="6" refY="3.5" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L7 3.5 L0 7 Z" fill="var(--accent)"/></marker></defs>
{kind==='split'&&<>
 {[['Training · 16 movies','Fit scaler + update weights','Gradient input: yes'],['Validation · 12 movies','Choose setup + checkpoint','Gradient input: no'],['Final test · separate','Assess the frozen choice','Not included in this lab']].map(([a,b,c],i)=><g><rect x={15+253*i} y="48" width="224" height="125" rx="7" class={i===0?'node node-accent':'node'}/><text x={127+253*i} y="84" text-anchor="middle" class="node-title">{a}</text><text x={127+253*i} y="119" text-anchor="middle" class="node-detail">{b}</text><text x={127+253*i} y="147" text-anchor="middle" class="node-detail">{c}</text></g>)}
 <text x="380" y="215" text-anchor="middle" class="node-title">Apply the training-fitted scaler to every split and to inference.</text><text x="380" y="244" text-anchor="middle" class="node-detail">Repeated tuning on validation is expected; it does not create independent test evidence.</text>
</>}
{kind==='loop'&&<>
 {[['Clear gradients','Fresh accumulation'],['Forward + loss','Predictions vs. labels'],['Backward','Compute derivatives'],['Optimizer step','Update parameters']].map(([a,b],i)=><g><rect x={12+190*i} y="30" width="167" height="85" rx="7" class={i===3?'node node-accent':'node'}/><text x={95+190*i} y="63" text-anchor="middle" class="node-title">{a}</text><text x={95+190*i} y="94" text-anchor="middle" class="node-detail">{b}</text></g>)}
 {[0,1,2].map(i=><line x1={180+190*i} x2={200+190*i} y1="73" y2="73" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end={'url(#'+id+'-arrow)'}/>)}
 <path d="M665 122V159H482" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none" marker-end={'url(#'+id+'-arrow)'}/><rect x="115" y="140" width="357" height="64" rx="7" class="node"/><text x="293" y="167" text-anchor="middle" class="node-title">Validate without weight updates</text><text x="293" y="191" text-anchor="middle" class="node-detail">Record losses → select checkpoint → check patience</text><text x="380" y="244" text-anchor="middle" class="node-detail">Framework evaluation mode and disabling gradient recording are separate controls.</text>
</>}
{kind==='diagnose'&&<>
 {[['Both losses stay high','Check data, gradients,','capacity, rate, and budget'],['Train ↓; validation ↑','Verify the gap, then test','stopping or regularization'],['Spikes or non-finite loss','Inspect scale, arithmetic,','gradients, and step size']].map(([a,b,c],i)=><g><rect x={15+253*i} y="38" width="224" height="128" rx="7" class="node node-accent"/><text x={127+253*i} y="77" text-anchor="middle" class="node-title">{a}</text><text x={127+253*i} y="114" text-anchor="middle" class="node-detail">{b}</text><text x={127+253*i} y="139" text-anchor="middle" class="node-detail">{c}</text></g>)}
 <text x="380" y="210" text-anchor="middle" class="node-title">Observe → form one hypothesis → change one thing → compare</text><text x="380" y="242" text-anchor="middle" class="node-detail">A better training score alone is not enough to accept a change.</text>
</>}
</svg></div><figcaption>{labels[kind][1]}</figcaption></figure>
